# Project Principles

This is a short index of stable cross-cutting engineering rules. It is not a broad project manual.

## What Belongs Here

- durable repo-wide principles
- doc ownership boundaries
- planning and context-hygiene defaults

## Core Principles

1. Keep docs layered instead of centralizing everything into one manual.
2. Keep every active repo-changing task resumable from a full active plan in `PLANS.md`.
3. Keep active work in `PLANS.md` and inactive future work in `docs/codex/TASKS_BACKLOG.md`.
4. Compact or archive completed plan detail only after validation and handoff are recorded.
5. Before committing, close completed active plans or record the exact resume point for unfinished work.
6. After compaction, interruption, resume, or milestone closure, reconcile plan, backlog, validation state, and statuses before code changes.
7. Do not leave stale next-work or milestone-status text in completed sections.
8. Remove completed backlog items by default once useful context is captured elsewhere.
9. Keep recurring mistakes in `docs/codex/AGENT_EXECUTION_PITFALLS.md` until they become durable principles.
10. Preserve the user's requested scope; conservative execution protects existing owners without silently reducing the outcome.
11. Keep passing noise out of the working context.
